  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 00)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "): a value computed with 40 digits is never reused where 60 are needed \
(review E15)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab7c1df6-54fd-4ba3-9701-d893ac295f2f"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:32-35 *)
(* finite-difference stencils {shift, weight} of d^m/dx^m at 0 *)
stencil[0, h_] := {{0, 1}};
stencil[1, h_] := {{h, 1/(2 h)}, {-h, -1/(2 h)}};
stencil[2, h_] := {{h, 1/h^2}, {0, -2/h^2}, {-h, 1/h^2}};\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"f3862559-6b61-4f99-bce3-5b77937cd97b"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:37-43 *)
(* (Laplacian_p)^n at p = 0 by nested central second differences over \
direction tuples (c1, ..., cn), and its normalisation
   N_n = (Laplacian)^n (p^2)^n = 4^n n! (d/2)_n (written here independently \
of Projection). For n >= 1, Richardson extrapolation
   (h, h/2) removes the O(h^2) error (review E19; at n = 1 it keeps the \
relative error below the tolerance when the coefficient is small). f is a \
function of the explicit d-vector p. *)
oracleLapNorm[n_, d_] := 4^n n! Pochhammer[d/2, n];
oracleLapStencil[f_, d_, n_, h_] := With[{units = IdentityMatrix[d], st = \
stencil[2, h]},
   Total[Flatten[Table[Times @@ sh[[All, 2]] f[ConstantArray[0, d] + \
Sum[sh[[i, 1]] units[[cs[[i]]]], {i, n}]], {cs, Tuples[Range[d], n]}, {sh, \
Tuples[st, n]}]]]];
oracleLaplacianN[f_, d_, n_, h_] := If[n == 0, oracleLapStencil[f, d, n, h], \
(4 oracleLapStencil[f, d, n, h/2] - oracleLapStencil[f, d, n, h])/3];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"d010a141-ea72-43fa-9d9a-14c10bed7ee0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The derivatives are central finite differences: ",
 StyleBox["stencil[m, h]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " lists the shifts and weights of d^m/dx^m at 0. For the momentum, (",
 StyleBox["\[Del]\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_p)",
 StyleBox["\:207f",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " is applied by nested second differences along every tuple of unit vectors \
(",
 StyleBox["Tuples",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", lesson 03), and the O(h",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") error is removed by Richardson extrapolation: (4 f(h/2) ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " f(h))/3. ",
 StyleBox["oracleLapNorm",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is N_n written again, independently of ",
 StyleBox["lapNorm",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " in Projection."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4333f784-e671-4396-91b4-f0499d73fbf3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["wedgeN[a_?VectorQ, b_?VectorQ] /; Length[a] == Length[b] == 2",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " evaluates ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " only once both vectors are explicit lists (",
 StyleBox["PatternTest",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 04)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "): before that, ",
 StyleBox["wedge[...]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " stays symbolic."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9cb40147-db37-441c-96ed-04856fbef072"],

Cell["3. Options and checks of the oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1b26a633-3127-4bb3-8056-a194f9938f4f"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:48-57 *)
Options[RunOracle] = {\"Dimensions\" -> Automatic, \"Tolerance\" -> 10^-8, \
\"Seed\" -> 1, \"ZeroFlows\" -> False};

RunOracle[eqs_, OptionsPattern[]] := Block[{$FRGModule = \"Oracle\"},
  Module[{t0 = AbsoluteTime[], closure, loops, v, reg, fields, hasG4, recs, \
checks = {}, warns = {}, results = {}, stage, tol = OptionValue[\"Tolerance\"],
    h = 10^-5, prec = 40, dims},
   validateStage[eqs, \"Equations\"];
   dims = Replace[OptionValue[\"Dimensions\"], Automatic -> \
If[eqs[\"Dimension\"] === 2, {2}, {2, 3}]];
   FRGAssert[\"Oracle.declaredDimension\", If[eqs[\"Dimension\"] === 2, dims \
=== {2}, ListQ[dims] && dims =!= {} && SubsetQ[{2, 3}, dims]], dims,
    If[eqs[\"Dimension\"] === 2, \"the dimension is declared: d = 2 only \
(\\\"Dimensions\\\" -> {2} or Automatic)\",
     \"\\\"Dimensions\\\" must be a non-empty subset of {2, 3}\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"fed3c9bc-e6d3-4743-b65b-888a3909b59b"],

Cell["showFailure[RunOracle[equations, \"Dimensions\" -> {4}]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2f34154e-6658-4ee4-9b3e-5cb6575d7b44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The validity conditions are also respected: the point is redrawn (up to 100 \
times, ",
 StyleBox["Break[]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " leaves the ",
 StyleBox["Do",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " loop) until the poles are causal, because the symbolic residues assume \
they are."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cceb0d8a-6bab-4863-adba-31c3272dc843"],

Cell["4. Saving and loading stages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"692686ba-fb1c-4d32-a4eb-8a25ecceee99"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Stages.wl:16-17 *)
StageFingerprints[s_Association] := Union[Flatten[{Lookup[s, \"Fingerprint\", \
{}], Lookup[s, \"Upstream\", {}],
     StageFingerprints /@ Select[Values[s], AssociationQ[#] && KeyExistsQ[#, \
\"Stage\"] &]}]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"d3835df9-eff7-4c82-99c2-e2da78b4ff0a"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Stages.wl:19-22 *)
SaveStage[stage_, file_String] := Block[{$FRGModule = \"Stages\"},
   FRGAssert[\"Stages.input\", AssociationQ[stage] && KeyExistsQ[stage, \
\"Stage\"] && KeyExistsQ[stage, \"Fingerprint\"], Head[stage], \"SaveStage \
takes a stage\"];
   validateStage[stage, stage[\"Stage\"]];
   Export[file, stage, \"WDX\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"8347aaa7-6be3-4255-bcb7-45cabf8b906d"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Stages.wl:24-38 *)
Options[LoadStage] = {\"Expect\" -> {}};
LoadStage[file_String, OptionsPattern[]] := Block[{$FRGModule = \"Stages\"},
  Module[{s, fps, exp = OptionValue[\"Expect\"], stale},
   FRGAssert[\"Stages.file\", FileExistsQ[file], file, \"no such file\"];
   s = Import[file, \"WDX\"];
   FRGAssert[\"Stages.input\", AssociationQ[s] && KeyExistsQ[s, \"Stage\"], \
Head[s], \"the file does not contain a stage\"];
   validateStage[s, s[\"Stage\"]];
   FRGAssert[\"Stages.expect\", AllTrue[exp, AssociationQ[#] && KeyExistsQ[#, \
\"Fingerprint\"] &], exp, \"\\\"Expect\\\" -> {stage, ...}\"];
   fps = StageFingerprints[s];
   stale = Select[exp, ! MemberQ[fps, #Fingerprint] &];
   FRGAssert[\"Stages.stale\", stale === {}, #Stage & /@ stale,
    \"the saved stage was not built from the current \" <> \
StringRiffle[#Stage & /@ stale, \", \"] <> \" stage(s): rebuild it\"];
   Print[\"LoadStage: \", s[\"Stage\"], \" stage, fingerprint \", \
StringTake[s[\"Fingerprint\"], 8], If[exp === {}, \"\",
     \", built from the current \" <> StringRiffle[#Stage & /@ exp, \", \
\"]]];
   s]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"bb8a07f1-b56a-4082-b917-196f86a58277"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Export and Import",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Export[file, expr, \"WDX\"]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " writes any expression in Mathematica's binary format; ",
 StyleBox["Import[file, \"WDX\"]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " reads it back identically.",
 "\n\n",
 "WDX stores the expression exactly, with symbols and their contexts, so a \
stage comes back as the same association. ",
 StyleBox["FileExistsQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " tests for a file; ",
 StyleBox["$TemporaryDirectory",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is the system's temporary folder."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"fd06bda8-a251-4000-850e-a47b4fd926a6"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"lessonKPZEquations.wdx\"}];
SaveStage[equations, file];
reloaded = LoadStage[file, \"Expect\" -> {kpzAnsatz, kpzRegulator, \
kpzSymmetries}];
reloaded === equations\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1e8f4894-e297-427e-9f9d-c038dfa4bb98"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["StageFingerprints",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " walks through every stage embedded in the saved one (recursively: a \
stage's values that are themselves stages) and collects their fingerprints \
and upstream lists. ",
 StyleBox["\"Expect\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " lists the stages you are working with now; each must be among them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a76fb143-227e-4206-887f-96c92eb28934"],

Cell["\<\
ansatzWithoutLambda = Block[{Print}, DefineAnsatz[kpzTheory, \"Density\" -> \
hbar (dt[h] - nuk lap[h]) - Dk hbar^2, \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, Dk}]];
showFailure[LoadStage[file, \"Expect\" -> {ansatzWithoutLambda}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"96b81d8d-173a-4785-a840-ebcb4c972908"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Persistence with a guard",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "Heavy models take minutes (shallow water) to hours (large p",
 StyleBox["\:2074",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " truncations), so saving intermediate stages matters. A saved file is also \
the classic source of silent errors: equations derived from last week's \
ansatz, loaded into today's notebook. ",
 StyleBox["LoadStage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " checks two things: the file was not modified (its own fingerprint), and it \
was built from the stages you are using now (",
 StyleBox["\"Expect\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "). Because every stage embeds its ancestors, the whole history is in the \
file and can be checked (",
 StyleBox["design/FRGDESIGN.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", Q13)."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"c67fe7ff-8610-42d9-925c-6578c32cf977"],

Cell["Exercises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7021c597-42b6-4f98-95a3-8f0a5a700e21"],

Cell["Exercise: A tighter tolerance", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bee0bc09-0eab-4a0a-a6ab-f9c42f74555f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run the oracle with ",
 StyleBox["\"Tolerance\" -> 10^-15",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and only d = 2. Does it pass? What sets the size of the error?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5646bc20-f9a1-4834-9e2a-7331541ebcc6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Solution", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"f6917961-ae1f-402c-94cc-f0cd2ec9a6d2"],

Cell["\<\
Block[{Print}, RunOracle[equations, \"Tolerance\" -> 10^-15, \"Dimensions\" \
-> {2}]][\"Results\"][[All, {\"Label\", \"Error\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7665b125-05dd-4772-81c4-9a09a604cde6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It passes: the errors are of order 10",
 StyleBox["\:207b\.b2\:2070",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", the size of the finite-difference error after Richardson extrapolation at \
the precision used."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85606cf7-c272-4d93-87bf-113f87f9ace0"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["Exercise: A modified file", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"78999e4d-5cf7-4f5e-9908-3639c67522c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Load the saved stage, change one key, save it under a new name with ",
 StyleBox["Export",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (not ",
 StyleBox["SaveStage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "), and load it with ",
 StyleBox["LoadStage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". Which check fails?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2255e608-7c0d-4082-a3b2-4879f6cdcc38"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Solution", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"4b7d4d9e-71b6-4aac-9582-9d736fb7e546"],

Cell["\<\
file2 = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \
\"lessonKPZEquationsEdited.wdx\"}];
Export[file2, Append[reloaded, \"Couplings\" -> {nuk}], \"WDX\"];
showFailure[LoadStage[file2]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"948c7a73-0dff-4cf9-9993-ce3f2aa865b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stage.fingerprint",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", from ",
 StyleBox["validateStage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (lesson 00): the content no longer matches the fingerprint stored with it. \
",
 StyleBox["SaveStage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " would have refused to write it in the first place."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30fb1167-9e88-4862-9df2-520515bd2fa6"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["Exercise: How much history is in a file", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"07ce2d39-34f9-4bb0-9fd9-6531efd37fbe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How many fingerprints does ",
 StyleBox["StageFingerprints[equations]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " find? Which stages do they belong to?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43f8fe67-1e6b-4acc-92a9-4c8bb18a26f0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Solution", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"f5dd5698-95e5-4148-b083-4fef00c7242c"],

Cell["\<\
{Length[StageFingerprints[equations]], Union[Cases[equations, \
KeyValuePattern[\"Stage\" -> s_String] :> s, {0, Infinity}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"664c4a2c-7e44-4504-92c3-9c880f4ae356"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every stage of the chain, from Theory to Equations. ",
 StyleBox["Cases",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["KeyValuePattern",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["Cases and level specifications",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 00)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 ") finds every embedded association with a ",
 StyleBox["\"Stage\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " key."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b243510-51dd-425b-9cd1-c1f9e1228cd6"]
}, Closed]]
},
CellContext->Notebook,
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
